base.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: transparent modular game-character animation source sheet, NEW separately painted hidden-overlap parts.
Input image 1 is only the exact character identity/outfit and four-direction reference; do NOT copy/cut/warp any full-body pose.
Subject: Brown wavy shoulder-length hair, brown eyes, small purple horns and purple ribbon ornaments; the exact purple-and-black gothic devil dress, detached purple sleeves, dark patterned thigh stockings, chunky purple buckle boots, two purple bat wings, and purple pointed tail from reference. No new props.
Paint a clean professional chibi anime RPG style matching reference, big expressive head, body/head ratio approximately2.3heads full standingheight. Consistent same scale and color across four independently drawn cardinal directions.
CRITICAL GRID: an exact8columns ×8rows grid with64 equal cells and broad transparent gutters. ONE isolated painted component centered in EACH cell. Each direction is16parts spanning TWO complete rows of8cells. Rows1-2 FRONT facing camera; rows3-4 TRUE RIGHT PROFILE, face/nose/ALL shoe toes point to the RIGHT EDGE of canvas; rows5-6 TRUE REAR, no face visible; rows7-8 TRUE LEFT PROFILE, nose/shoe toes point to LEFT EDGE. Right and left must be separately drawn correct anatomy, not both facingleft. Side torso/hips narrower because true profile anatomy; do not draw3quarter front pelvis under a side head.
For EACH16part block, cells in exact reading order:
1 isolated head with face and full scalp/bangs (no torso/neck/body);2 separate back hair cap/length;
3 upper garment torso from neck to waist ONLY, NO arms and NO skirt/lower garment;
4 pelvis/lower garment from waist including existing skirt/robe hem if present, NO legs/feet;
5 anatomicalLEFT upperarm/sleeve shoulder-to-elbow;6 LEFT forearm/sleeve+hand elbow-to-fingers;
7 RIGHT upperarm/sleeve shoulder-to-elbow;8 RIGHT forearm/sleeve+hand;
9 LEFT thigh/upper trouser leg hip-to-knee;10 LEFT shin/lower trouser+shoe knee-to-SOLE;
11 RIGHT thigh;12 RIGHT shin+shoe;
13-16 extras as specified next: Slots13 and14 are separately painted LEFT and RIGHT bat wings, attached only at their root; slot15 is tail base from waist to middle joint; slot16 is pointed tail tip. Keep wings and tail separate from torso/head.
Every arm/leg has a rounded painted overlap extension at shoulder, elbow, hip and knee, hidden under neighboring pieces after assembly. Paint complete underlying limbs/boots even where dress hides them. Upper and lower limbs must be separate components, never a whole arm or whole leg. Shoes include actual soles touching the measured bottom. Profiles use side noses and side toes; rear shoes show heels.
No assembled bodies, no skeleton drawings, no labels/text/numbers, no shadows on background, no checkerboard, no decorative particles, no colored fringe or red marks. Transparent RGBA background, clean antialiased edges. Keep all64 painted components completely separated by ample clear space, never touching neighboring cells.
